@startuml
title Template Method / Hook Method

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Define algorithm skeleton and let subclasses redefine steps.

**Motivation**:
Common process with customizable steps.

**Applicability**:
Fixed workflow with flexible steps; framework extension points.

**Participants**:
AbstractClass holds template; ConcreteClass overrides primitives.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Enforces sequence; reuse; inversion of control.
Cons: Inheritance coupling; less flexible than composition.

**Implementation Notes**:
Hooks (optional steps) via default no-op implementations.

**Known Uses**:
JUnit lifecycle (@Before, @After hooks conceptually template-like).
Servlet lifecycle methods (init, service, destroy).

**Related Patterns**:
Strategy (composition), Factory Method (step override), Hook methods.

endlegend

abstract class AbstractClass {
  +templateMethod()
  #primitiveOp1()
  #primitiveOp2()
}

class ConcreteClassA
class ConcreteClassB

AbstractClass <|-- ConcreteClassA
AbstractClass <|-- ConcreteClassB
@enduml